                            5
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَوَطَّنَتْ نَفْسُهُ عَلَى الشَّىْءِ</span></b> 
                        , and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَهُ</span>, <i>He undertook the thing, and submitted to it;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَحَمَّلَتْ</span>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَذَلَّتْ لَهُ</span> (ISd, in TA) [see also 2 and 10] <i>his
mind, or he, became disposed and subjected to do
the thing;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَهَّدَتْ</span>. (K [in the CK, for
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَوَطُّنَهَا تَمَهُّدَهَا</span>, is put <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَوَطَّنَهَا تَمَهَّدَهَا</span>].)

